    "title": "Yankees' Anthony Volpe hears loud boos after fitting cap to brutal ALDS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mark W. Sanchez ,\n4 hours ago\nHeroes and zeros from the Yankees’ 5-2 season-ending loss to the Blue Jays in ALDS Game 4 at the Stadium.\nHero Cam Schlittler against a bullpen game seemed like a matchup until Johnny Wholestaff was put into motion. Eight different Blue Jays pitchers held the Yankees to six hits and two runs while striking out nine.\nThe ugly truth that you can’t ignore about these high-priced Yankees\nZero After an excellent wild-card series, Anthony Volpe sunk to 1-for-15 with 11 strikeouts in the ALDS. He chased Strike 3 in the seventh inning and heard loud boos on the way to the dugout. In the ninth, Aaron Boone sat Volpe for pinch-hitter Jasson Domínguez.\nCam Schlittler second postseason act was good — but not good enough to save Yankees’ season\nBlue Jays right fielder Nathan Lukes hits a two-run single during the seventh inning against the Toronto Blue Jays in Game four of the ALDS on Wednesday. JASON SZENES/ NY POST CLICK HERE TO SIGN UP FOR OUR MORNING REPORT NEWSLETTER\nUnsung hero There wasn’t a bigger hit than Nathan Lukes’ two-run single poked into left-center to allow Toronto some breathing room in the seventh.\nStat: 16 Years without a Yankees World Series championship.\nFor the latest in sports, top headlines, breaking news and more, visit nypost.com/sports/",
